{
  "case_id": "C03",
  "audience": "School governors and parents",
  "target_duration_s": 90,
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat": "The question",
      "narration": "Can portable air cleaners keep more children in class? One local authority looked at that over a single winter term. Twenty-two primary classrooms were each given two portable HEPA units; eighteen other classrooms in the same authority carried on as usual.",
      "on_screen": "Title: Do HEPA air cleaners cut respiratory absence? Split graphic: 22 classrooms with units, 18 without",
      "claim_refs": ["design", "abstract"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "What the numbers showed",
      "narration": "In the classrooms with units, absence coded as respiratory illness fell from 4.9 to 3.6 percent of pupil-days. In the comparison classrooms it fell from 4.7 to 4.4 percent. After allowing for that background change, the difference was about one percentage point, with a range running from 1.9 points down to just 0.1.",
      "on_screen": "Simple bar chart of before and after for both groups; caption: difference-in-differences -1.0 pp (95% CI -1.9 to -0.1)",
      "claim_refs": ["results_table", "abstract"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "How classrooms were chosen",
      "narration": "Here is the important part. Classrooms were not allocated at random. School leaders decided which rooms got units, based on available floor space. So the two groups may have differed from the start, and they did: baseline ventilation was not the same in both.",
      "on_screen": "Icon of a floor plan with a Chosen, not randomised label; note: baseline ventilation differed",
      "claim_refs": ["limitations[0]", "limitations[4]", "methods"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "Everyone knew",
      "narration": "Nobody was blinded. Teachers and pupils could see the units, and the office staff entering the absence codes knew which classrooms had them. The outcome is an administrative code in the school system, not a lab-confirmed infection.",
      "on_screen": "Screen showing an attendance code being entered; label: unblinded, no laboratory confirmation",
      "claim_refs": ["limitations[1]", "limitations[3]", "methods"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "One term, one place",
      "narration": "And it ran for one eleven-week term, in one local authority, during one respiratory season. Absence swings a lot from term to term, so a single season cannot tell us much on its own.",
      "on_screen": "Calendar strip highlighting a single 11-week winter term",
      "claim_refs": ["limitations[2]", "abstract"]
    },
    {
      "beat": "What to take from it",
      "narration": "So: a small, encouraging signal, but not proof that the units caused the drop. The authors say the same, and call for a randomised trial. Treat this as a reason to watch the evidence, not a reason to commit to a purchase.",
      "on_screen": "Summary card: Promising but not proof. Randomised evaluation needed.",
      "claim_refs": ["author_conclusion"]
    }
  ]
}
